source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-23
observed: The same split runs without a visible text part, and Jira shows the error span for the target the backslash left behind; jiro keeps the bracket text literal and warns.
-- input.jira --
[http://x/a\|b]
-- rendered.html --
<p><span class="error">&#91;http://x/a\|b&#93;</span></p>
-- want.md --
\[http://x/a\\|b\]
-- warnings.json --
[
 {
  "Line": 1,
  "Column": 1,
  "Construct": "link",
  "Reason": "backslash before a Jira link separator leaves a target Jira cannot resolve; complete link remains literal"
 }
]
